course: dictionary
lesson: 12389
title: Cultivated: land, plants and people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. «The cultivated fields were full of golden wheat.» Fields full of wheat are farmland that people have dug, planted and looked after, so cultivated means farmed.
explain: «The cultivated strawberries in the shop were huge and sweet.» The word cultivated tells you that people grew the strawberries on purpose, so they were not wild ones in a hedge. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Cultivated can also describe a person. «Her cultivated manners impressed everyone at dinner.» Here it means polite and well educated, someone who knows about art, music and books. As a verb form of cultivate, «She cultivated roses» means she grew them over time.
fact: Cultivated means dug, planted and looked after for growing crops, as in «cultivated land».
fact: A cultivated plant has been grown by people on purpose, not wild.
fact: A cultivated person is well educated, polite and knows about art, music and books.
fact: As a verb form, «cultivated» means grew or developed, as in «He cultivated a friendship».
fact: The first farmers cultivated wheat and barley.
exercise: «The cultivated fields were full of golden wheat.» What does cultivated mean here? | Covered in snow | Made of stone | *Dug, planted and looked after for growing crops | Wild and covered in weeds
exercise: «Her cultivated manners impressed everyone at dinner.» What does cultivated suggest about her? | Loud and rude | *Polite and well educated | Tired after a long walk | Lost and confused
exercise: «He cultivated a friendship with his new neighbour.» What does cultivated mean here? | Forgot | Shouted at | Dug up | *Grew or developed
test: In history lessons, the first farmers ____ wheat and barley. Which word fits best? | *Cultivated | Forgot | Painted | Hunted
test: «The cultivated strawberries were grown on a farm, not in the wild.» Why does the author use cultivated? | *Because people grew them on purpose | Because they were hidden | Because they were rotten | Because they came from the sea
exam: «She cultivated a love of music, reading and art.» What does cultivated mean here? | *Grew or developed over time | Broke into pieces | Was very quick at running | Dug up the garden
